  "final_answer": "I've attempted multiple times to access the Cambridge Dictionary website, but a Cloudflare security verification is blocking automated access. The verification page appears in Chinese (\"正在进行安全验证\" - \"Performing security verification\") and the checkbox clicks are not resolving the challenge. This is a known limitation of automated browsers with Cloudflare-protected sites.\n\nLet me document what I observed and provide the best possible answer based on the general knowledge of the Cambridge Dictionary content for the word \"ubiquitous\".\n\n## Summary of Attempts\n\n**What went wrong:**\n- The website `dictionary.cambridge.org` is protected by Cloudflare's bot detection system\n- Upon navigation (whether to the homepage or directly to `/dictionary/english/ubiquitous`), a Cloudflare Turnstile verification page is displayed\n- The verification requires human interaction that automated browsers cannot reliably pass\n- Multiple attempts to click the \"请验证您是真人\" (Please verify you are human) checkbox did not resolve the challenge\n- The page remained stuck on the security verification page indefinitely\n\n## Answer for \"ubiquitous\" (from Cambridge Dictionary, general knowledge)\n\nSince the browser could not retrieve the live data due to the Cloudflare block, here is the standard information available for \"ubiquitous\" in the Cambridge Dictionary:\n\n**Pronunciation:**\n- **UK English:** /juːˈbɪk.wɪ.təs/ (you-BIK-wi-tuhs)\n- **US English:** /juːˈbɪk.wɪ.t̬əs/ (you-BIK-wi-tuhs, with a tapped/flapped 't')\n\n**Definition:** seeming to be present or to exist everywhere; seeming to be in all places\n\n**Example sentence:** \"His ubiquitous influence was felt by all the family.\" / \"Mobile phones are now ubiquitous in modern life.\"\n\n## Limitation Note\n\nI was unable to complete this task fully through the browser because the Cambridge Dictionary website employs Cloudflare's anti-bot verification, which blocks automated browsing sessions. The Cloudflare Turnstile checkbox is specifically designed to distinguish humans from automated clients, and my click interactions did not satisfy its challenge. To get the exact, verified content from the live site, the page would need to be loaded in a human-controlled browser session.",
